# {{.AppName}}

A [trails](https://github.com/asimmons91/trails) application.

## Getting started

    mise install
{{if eq .AssetsStrategy "bundler"}}    mise run deps
{{end}}    trails migrate up
    mise run dev

This starts the app with live reload (via [air](https://github.com/air-verse/air))
at http://127.0.0.1:3000.

## Database

This app uses trails' `pack` ORM with {{if eq .Database "sqlite"}}SQLite{{else if eq .Database "postgres"}}Postgres{{else}}MySQL{{end}}. Migrations live in
`db/migrations` and are managed with the `trails` CLI:

    trails migrate create <name>   # generate a new migration
    trails migrate up              # apply pending migrations
    trails migrate down            # roll back the last migration

A starter migration and example model (`app/models/example.go`) are already
included — run `trails migrate up` before starting the app for the first time.

Type-safe field/relation query helpers (`ExampleFields.Title.Eq("x")`, etc.)
can be generated from your models instead of hand-written:

    trails generate fields    # (re)generate app/models/trails_fields_gen.go with type-safe *Fields helpers
{{if ne .Database "sqlite"}}
This app expects a {{if eq .Database "postgres"}}Postgres{{else}}MySQL{{end}} server reachable with the
credentials in `config/application.toml` (override per-environment in
`config/environments/*.toml`, or via `TRAILS_DATABASE_*` env vars). For local
development:

{{if eq .Database "postgres"}}    docker run -d -p 5432:5432 -e POSTGRES_USER=postgres -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres -e POSTGRES_DB=app_development postgres:16-alpine
{{else}}    docker run -d -p 3306:3306 -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=root -e MYSQL_DATABASE=app_development mysql:8
{{end}}{{end}}
## Credentials

This app has encrypted credentials for the `development` environment already:
`config/credentials/development.toml.enc` (safe to commit) plus
`config/credentials/development.key` (gitignored — the master key, distribute
it out-of-band). Manage them with:

    trails credentials edit --environment=development   # decrypt, open $EDITOR, re-encrypt
    trails credentials show --environment=development    # print decrypted contents

Other environments (`production`, `test`, ...) get their own key + encrypted
file the first time you run `trails credentials edit -e <environment>`. In
deploys without a key file on disk, set `TRAILS_MASTER_KEY` instead.

Any TOML entry whose shape matches `Config` (e.g. `[database]\npassword =
"..."`) is layered onto the loaded config automatically — a good place to
move secrets like the database password out of plaintext
`config/environments/*.toml`. Anything else goes through
`trails.LoadCredentials[config.Credentials]`.

## Assets
{{if eq .AssetsStrategy "bundler"}}
This app builds its frontend with esbuild (JS) and Tailwind CLI (CSS) from
`app/frontend/`. Build scripts live in `package.json`:

    mise run deps      # npm install
    mise run assets    # runs build:js + build:css, then fingerprints into public/assets

`mise run build`/`mise run dev` already depend on `assets`, so this normally
happens automatically.
{{else}}
This app ships with a plain, unbundled `public/assets/app.css` and no frontend
build tooling. To add a bundler (Tailwind, esbuild, ...) later:

1. Add a `package.json` with your build scripts.
2. Run `trails assets build --scripts=<your-scripts>` to fingerprint the
   output into `public/assets` and regenerate `manifest.json`.
3. Switch `AssetsStrategy` in `app/boot.go` to `trails.AssetsStrategyBundler`.

This app defaults to the `importmap` asset strategy. Pin a JS package with:

    trails importmap pin <package>
{{end}}
## Optional subsystems

trails also ships optional, opt-in subsystems not wired into this app by
default:

- **jobs** — background job registry + backends (`github.com/asimmons91/trails/jobs`)
- **channels** — SSE/ActionCable-style pub-sub (`github.com/asimmons91/trails/channels`)

Both are mountable as a `trails.Spur`. See their package docs to add them.

## Project layout

    app/
      boot.go               entrypoint wiring (config, db, routes)
      controllers/           request handlers + route table
      models/                pack-backed models
      views/                 html/template views (Rails-style controller/action convention)
    config/                  application.toml + per-environment overrides
    db/
      db.go                  DB connection
      migrations/             migration files
    public/                  embedded static + asset files
